# Git: branches before multi-file work

Full policy: [docs/BRANCHING.md](../../docs/BRANCHING.md)

## Rules

1. **Never commit directly to the integration branch (`{INTEGRATION_BRANCH}`)** — always branch first
2. **One task = one branch** — name: `feat/{id}-description`
3. **Collision check first** — `cams_query` what's `In Progress` in this repo and what it touches before cutting the branch. Same file/surface, no declared order → add `depends_on` or ask which goes first, don't silently branch and hope
4. **One concern per branch** — don't mix unrelated areas
5. **Push the branch** after commits — `git push -u origin <branch>`
6. **Merge via GitHub PR** — squash merge preferred
7. **No agent merges or deletes branches autonomously** — always propose via PR or ask first
8. **No force-push to `{INTEGRATION_BRANCH}`/`main`** without explicit human instruction
9. **Never commit** `.env`, secrets, or machine-local IDE state

## Branch naming

| Prefix | Use for | Example |
|--------|---------|---------|
| `feat/` | New feature | `feat/{PROJECT_NAME}-42-auth-flow` |
| `fix/` | Bug fix | `fix/{PROJECT_NAME}-51-secret-rotation` |
| `chore/` | Tooling/deps | `chore/update-deps` |
| `docs/` | Docs only | `docs/api-guide` |
| `park/` | Shelved/parked work | `park/apiV2-explore` |

## Quick start

```bash
git fetch origin && git checkout {INTEGRATION_BRANCH} && git pull origin {INTEGRATION_BRANCH}
git checkout -b feat/{id}-short-description
# ... work ...
git push -u origin feat/{id}-short-description
# Open PR on GitHub
```

In Claude Code, the `task-kickoff` skill runs all of this (claim, collision check, branch origin, migration-number check) automatically — see `.claude/skills/task-kickoff/SKILL.md`.
